<h2>Reveal: add content on a click</h2>

<p>
  Wrap anything in <c><step></c> and it stays hidden until the next click. Nothing moves when it appears:
  the space is reserved.
</p>

<step>
  <p>This text appeared on the first click.</p>
</step>

<step>
  <ul>
    <li>and a list</li>
    <li>on the second</li>
  </ul>
</step>

<step>
  <code lang=typescript>
    const clicks = 3; // the code block came last
  </code>
</step>

<step>
  <p>A list can appear bullet by bullet: write <c><ul steps></c>.</p>
</step>

<ul steps>
  <li>first click</li>
  <li>second click</li>
  <li>third click</li>
</ul>

<notes>
  Works for text, lists, images, video, charts and code blocks. Frames of a code block count as clicks too. `<step at=3>` names the click.
</notes>
